The above-stated criminal proceedings, including the summoning order, were then challenged by respondent nos.2 and 3 before the High Court of Judicature at Allahabad on various grounds,
including (i) it was a civil dispute, that had been wrongfully given the colour of a criminal offence;
(ii) the allotment letter contained an arbitration clause and hence no criminal proceedings could be initiated.
